scope: |
  ONE arm of renderTerm in RustCodeWalk: the `++` list/Vec concat emission (~L3499-3508), which
  builds `[a, b].concat()` and MOVES both operands, so reusing a list after `++` is E0382.
  Changed to `[&(a)[..], &(b)[..]].concat()`. Not touching member/receiver-type rendering — that
  is co-tenant `rust-total-seq-members`, announced in the room.
  Widened to tests/e2e/build-rust-refuses-loudly.sh: it already pays for cargo and already builds
  a list program against the default lane, so the operand-reuse row belongs there rather than in
  a new CI step.
next: verify the rebuilt toolchain emits the borrowed form and the program runs 5/15
